From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 16:25:40 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] hwcomposer: v11: log a prepare or set failure once, not per frame

HWC_PLUGIN_EXPECT_ZERO logged every failing prepare() and set(), so a
module that fails one of them on every frame wrote a journal line per
frame. Qualcomm's display-caf HWC for msm8960, which the HP TouchPad's
msm8660 uses, does: hwc_set() walks the display list up to and including
numDisplays, the entry past the end lands in its "-EINVAL" default case,
and as the last one it decides the return value, although the primary
display was drawn and committed. On the TouchPad that was up to a dozen
"err in present returned -22" lines a second.

Log a failure when its code first shows up and again only when it
changes.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
--- a/hwcomposer_backend_v11.cpp
+++ b/hwcomposer_backend_v11.cpp
@@ -155,14 +155,31 @@
 
     QPA_HWC_TIMING_SAMPLE(syncTime);
 
+    /*
+     * A failure is logged when it first shows up, not for every frame. Some modules fail every
+     * set without anything being wrong: Qualcomm's display-caf HWC for msm8960 (the HP TouchPad's
+     * msm8660 uses it) walks the display list up to and including numDisplays, and the entry past
+     * the end ends in its "-EINVAL" default case after the primary display has been committed.
+     * Logged per frame, that was up to a dozen journal lines a second.
+     */
+    static int lastPrepareErr = 0, lastSetErr = 0;
+
     int err = hwcdevice->prepare(hwcdevice, num_displays, mlist);
-    HWC_PLUGIN_EXPECT_ZERO(err);
+    if (err != lastPrepareErr) {
+        if (err != 0)
+            qWarning("QPA-HWC: prepare returned %i (logged again only when it changes)", err);
+        lastPrepareErr = err;
+    }
 
     QPA_HWC_TIMING_SAMPLE(prepareTime);
 
     QSystrace::begin("graphics", "QPA::set", "");
     err = hwcdevice->set(hwcdevice, num_displays, mlist);
-    HWC_PLUGIN_EXPECT_ZERO(err);
+    if (err != lastSetErr) {
+        if (err != 0)
+            qWarning("QPA-HWC: set returned %i (logged again only when it changes)", err);
+        lastSetErr = err;
+    }
     QSystrace::end("graphics", "QPA::set", "");
 
     QPA_HWC_TIMING_SAMPLE(setTime);
